**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** Under 001 §B and .spec-md §3.7, startup MUST identify every row before confirmation. In OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs, CatalogueImportContext MUST gain hashManifest : CatalogueManifest -> Result<ContentHash, CatalogueImportError>, now : unit -> CatalogueImportTime and openCatalogue : FolderName -> CatalogueProxy. OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueImportStore.fs MUST supply manifestHash, the clock and CatalogueProxy.create at the IO boundary; tests MUST replace the clock. PendingCatalogueImport MUST contain entry : CatalogueImportLogEntry and decisions : ImportDecision list. FolderImportResult MUST have CatalogueUnchanged of CatalogueImportLogEntry, CatalogueImported of CatalogueImportLogEntry (a settled result), and CatalogueAwaitsChoices of PendingCatalogueImport. FolderImportReport MUST hold folder and outcome; StartupImportReport MUST hold folders and expose pending in folder order. importFolder MUST read and hash the manifest and return CatalogueUnchanged without reading entry files or writing anything when its logged hash matches. Otherwise it MUST read the catalogue, obtain every decision through importCatalogue, and return CatalogueAwaitsChoices containing all rows, including Reuse and unrelated additions. It MUST NOT apply a row, retire an entry or log the changed hash. importOnStart MUST process the shipped folder first, then logged folders other than the built-in catalogue in log order, returning each folder error without stopping other folders; a loggedImports failure MUST be returned. No retries or extra cache are added. In CatalogueImportContract, both implementations MUST exercise the five declared facts: (a) first startup returns all rows pending with no writes; after the fixture explicitly applies every default and logs the successful import, the next unchanged start MUST skip entry reads even if an entry file was deleted; (b) a changed built-in version MUST leave held versions and latest unchanged before confirmation, then add the new version and move latest after explicit apply and log; (c) a mixed collision, Reuse and new-source catalogue MUST return all rows pending, write neither source nor log, and do the same after cancellation and another start; (d) logged folders MUST be reported in order, a changed valid folder pending and an unreadable folder an error, without either being logged; (e) after confirmation, user entries MUST retain the version/latest/retirement safeguards of the per-entry table. Fresh GUID-named folders MUST live under AppContext.BaseDirectory/CatalogueImportTests. Step 99 MUST replace the fixture's explicit apply-and-log sequence with settle, preserving the same observations.

**Acceptance.** After startup identifies a changed catalogue, every decision row MUST remain pending and library entries, latest pointers, lifecycle and import log MUST stay unchanged until confirmation; unchanged manifest hashes MUST skip entry reads; both-store CatalogueImportContract facts and the required gates MUST pass.
